<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tamil Nadu</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tamil Nadu is a state of south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coromandel-coast">Coromandel Coast</a>, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chennai">Chennai</a>. It formed the core of ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tamilakam">Tamilakam</a>, ruled by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chera-dynasty">Cheras</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chola-empire">Cholas</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pandya-dynasty">Pandyas</a>, and is known for its great <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> temples and classical Tamil literature. The state took its present borders as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madras-state">Madras State</a> in 1956 on linguistic lines and was renamed Tamil Nadu in 1969.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tamil-nadu.jpg" alt="Tamil Nadu" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: https://www.flickr.com/photos/pnglife/ · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mamallapuram_view.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
